---
display_code: "7.2"
title: Emerging Technologies
paper: "2"
order: 20
---

Emerging technologies covers the digital capabilities that have moved from
research into mainstream commercial use within the last decade, and those
currently on the cusp. Machine learning, the Internet of Things, blockchain,
and quantum approaches sit alongside less glamorous but equally consequential
shifts such as edge computing and serverless architectures.

The core of this area is not the novelty of any single technology. It is the
ability to reason about what a technology makes possible, what it costs, and
where its limits lie, rather than treating it as a buzzword to list on an
exam paper.
